  m_Name: snowdrop
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::FlowerData
  id: snowdrop
  displayName: Snow drop
  scientificName: 'Galanthus nivalis '
  markerImageName: snowdrop
  description: The common snowdrop is a small perennial bulb that flowers near the
    end of winter. Each slender stem usually carries one nodding white flower with
    three larger outer petals and smaller inner petals marked with green. Its narrow
    leaves emerge through cold ground, sometimes even through snow, making it one
    of the earliest signs of approaching spring.
  origin: "Europe \u2014 from the Pyrenees eastward to Ukraine"
  meaning: Hope, renewal, purity, consolation and the arrival of spring. Because
    it flowers during winter, it is often viewed as a symbol of perseverance.
  habitat: Deciduous woodlands, forest edges, riverbanks, meadows and shaded gardens
    with moist, fertile and well-drained soil.
  birthflower: January
  floweringSeason: January to March, depending on the local climate
  sunlight: Partial shade is ideal, especially beneath deciduous trees. It can tolerate
    winter sun while the trees have no leaves.
  watering: Keep the soil moderately moist during active growth. Avoid letting it
    remain waterlogged. Once the leaves die back and the bulb becomes dormant, only
    minimal additional watering is required.
  difficulty: Easy
  arScale: 0.05
  flowerImage: {fileID: 0}
